 13 │ theorem leftOut (a: Nat) (b: Nat): range (a + 1) b = [a, b, 1] := rfl
    │                                                                   ─┬─  
    │                                                                    ╰─── `range (a + 1) b` and `[a, b, 1]` aren't equal
    │ 
    │ Note 1: computing the left side gives `[a + 1, b, 1]`
    │ 
    │ Note 2: `rfl` proves `a = b` only when both sides compute to the same value
    │ 
    │ Note 3: this statement is false; a counterexample:
    │           a = 0
    │           b = 0
    │         `range (a + 1) b = [a, b, 1]` is false:
    │           left:  [1, 0, 1]
    │           right: [0, 0, 1]
    │           first difference at [0]: 1 vs 0
